y?","b":"9 marks","t":["PPP::OCR::J411","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"OCR GCSE History J411 – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-hist-J411-mark:764cedb14662bf76b986","f":"What is the AO1/AO2 split for J411/14 Question 2?","b":"AO1 6 marks; AO2 3 marks","t":["PPP::OCR::J411","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"OCR GCSE History J411 – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-hist-J411-mark:8018f250a2bc08b68568","f":"How many marks are available for J411/14 Question 5, the judgement question?","b":"18 marks","t":["PPP::OCR::J411","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"OCR GCSE History J411 – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-hist-J411-mark:24bbd857916c52b5061f","f":"What is the AO1/AO2 split for J411/14 Question 5?","b":"AO1 6 marks; AO2 12 marks","t":["PPP::OCR::J411","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"OCR GCSE History J411 – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-hist-J411-mark:29f42f78a33104b32b82","f":"How should a J411 source inference answer use the source?","b":"Model answer: Make a valid inference, support it with source detail, then use contextual knowledge. Marking points: Inference; precise detail; relevant context. Common trap: Copying the source without explaining what it suggests.","t":["PPP::OCR::J411","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"OCR GCSE History J411 – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-hist-J411-mark:e34a08cca667da87254e","f":"How should a J411 organised summary be constructed?","b":"Model answer: Organise examples around a historical connection such as change or cause. Marking points: Accurate examples; clear connection; logical reasoning. Common trap: Listing events without analysing their relationship.","t":["PPP::OCR::J411","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"OCR GCSE History J411 – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-hist-J411-mark:f7f1844dcfc564058027","f":"How should a J411 explanation answer develop a cause?","b":"Model answer: Explain how a reason led to the outcome, supported by precise evidence. Marking points: Accurate knowledge; causal link; developed explanation. Common trap: Naming causes without explaining their effects.","t":["PPP::OCR::J411","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"OCR GCSE History J411 – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-hist-J411-mark:220ab715b4f66b515fef","f":"How should a J411 18-mark judgement answer reach the highest levels?","b":"Model answer: Explain evidence on both sides and reach a supported judgement. Marking points: Strong knowledge; developed reasoning; balanced argument; clear judgement. Common trap: One-sided assertions or a list of facts.","t":["PPP::OCR::J411","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"OCR GCSE History J411 – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"},{"k":"ppp-gcse-hist-J411-mark:93795f9272b8e73ece1a","f":"How should a J411/33 15-mark usefulness answer assess sources and interpretations?","b":"Model answer: Assess the interpretation and sources for the stated issue using context. Marking points: AO1 context; source analysis (AO3); interpretation analysis (AO4); supported judgement. Common trap: Asserting bias or discussing only one item.","t":["PPP::OCR::J411","PPP::Deck::mark_scheme","PPP::Paper::assessment-skills","PPP::Topic::assessment-skills","PPP::Class::mark_scheme"],"p":"OCR GCSE History J411 – Exam technique::Assessment skills::Assessment skills:: Assessment skills"}]$j$::jsonb) as x(k text,f text,b text,t text[],p text) left join public.flashcard_catalogue_items i on i.catalogue_id='OCR_GCSE_HIST_J411_MARK' and i.stable_key=x.k left join public.flashcard_catalogue_material m on m.catalogue_id='OCR_GCSE_HIST_J411_MARK' and m.version_id='ba4c8b74-2e1e-40d6-8ed1-b024a0fea654'::uuid and m.catalogue_card_id=i.id;
